A young Indian prince in flowing silk robes sits peacefully beneath a sprawling Bodhi tree in an ancient palace garden, rendered in Marc Chagall's dreamlike style with floating elements and jewel-toned colors of deep blues, purples, and golds. The prince has a serene expression, eyes half-closed in contemplation. Around him, whimsical elements drift through the air: lotus flowers, peacock feathers, and delicate mango blossoms defying gravity. The palace of the Shakya kingdom rises in the misty background with ornate domes and spires. Parts of the scene appear deliberately unfinished, with visible sketchy pencil lines and areas of bare canvas showing through, as if inviting completion. Soft golden light bathes the composition, creating an ethereal, storybook quality perfect for children.
